{"id":"ux-wireframes","title":"UI/UX: wireframes and prototypes","subject":"UI/UX design","label":"UI/UX design","exams":[],"language":"en","seconds":162,"duration":161.89,"audio":"voice.mp3","words":461,"sections":[{"id":"hook","title":"The puzzle","start":0,"end":12.445},{"id":"explain","title":"Wireframes","start":12.445,"end":50.595},{"id":"explain2","title":"Flow and prototype","start":50.595,"end":82.105},{"id":"example","title":"Login example","start":82.105,"end":106.955},{"id":"check","title":"Quick check","start":106.955,"end":116.745},{"id":"answer","title":"The answer","start":116.745,"end":122.285},{"id":"mistakes","title":"Common mistakes","start":122.285,"end":142.155},{"id":"recap","title":"Recap and tip","start":142.155,"end":161.89}],"lines":[{"s":0,"a":0.5,"b":4.79,"text":"Have you ever tapped a button on a website and wondered why it was so hard to find?","w":[0.52,0.66,0.82,1.06,1.38,1.46,1.76,1.86,1.94,2.74,2.88,3.28,3.58,3.66,3.84,4.06,4.26,4.4]},{"s":0,"a":5.24,"b":5.92,"text":"I'm Kora.","w":[5.36,5.54]},{"s":0,"a":6.22,"b":12.02,"text":"Today I'll show you the simple drawings and clickable drafts that fix that long before anyone writes a line of code.","w":[6.26,6.86,7.04,7.24,7.38,7.52,7.86,8.32,8.48,8.92,9.38,9.58,9.88,10.12,10.42,10.76,11.06,11.34,11.42,11.6,11.72]},{"s":1,"a":12.87,"b":15.4,"text":"A wireframe is a simple outline of a screen.","w":[12.94,13.04,13.8,13.92,14.06,14.5,14.88,14.98,15.04]},{"s":1,"a":15.7,"b":20.29,"text":"It uses boxes, lines and labels to show what goes where and what matters most.","w":[15.74,15.92,16.22,16.96,17.4,17.54,17.94,18.1,18.34,18.5,18.8,19.18,19.32,19.52,19.86]},{"s":1,"a":20.59,"b":24.11,"text":"There are no colours, no real pictures and no final fonts.","w":[20.59,20.78,20.94,21.16,21.74,21.96,22.22,22.86,23.06,23.3,23.66]},{"s":1,"a":24.41,"b":26.5,"text":"Think of it as the blueprint of a house.","w":[24.46,24.7,24.8,24.98,25.12,25.24,25.82,25.96,26.04]},{"s":1,"a":26.8,"b":29.08,"text":"It shows the structure, not the decoration.","w":[26.84,26.98,27.26,27.36,28.18,28.38,28.5]},{"s":1,"a":29.38,"b":33.23,"text":"Low fidelity means rough and quick, like pencil and paper.","w":[29.46,29.72,30.28,30.62,31.08,31.28,32.02,32.3,32.74,32.88]},{"s":1,"a":33.53,"b":36.09,"text":"High fidelity means close to the finished look.","w":[33.6,33.88,34.42,34.82,35.22,35.34,35.48,35.82]},{"s":1,"a":36.39,"b":39.09,"text":"Start rough because it is fast and cheap.","w":[36.5,36.84,37.5,37.78,37.9,38.08,38.56,38.72]},{"s":1,"a":39.39,"b":41.55,"text":"You can try five ideas in ten minutes.","w":[39.4,39.54,39.72,40.02,40.36,40.78,40.88,41.1]},{"s":1,"a":41.85,"b":46.23,"text":"People then give honest feedback on the structure instead of arguing about colours.","w":[41.88,42.24,42.46,42.74,43.14,43.64,43.72,43.84,44.62,44.94,45.08,45.46,45.7]},{"s":1,"a":46.53,"b":50.17,"text":"So a wireframe answers one question: what is this screen for?","w":[46.62,46.82,46.9,47.54,47.96,48.14,49.12,49.32,49.44,49.6,49.94]},{"s":2,"a":51.02,"b":55.18,"text":"A user flow is the path of screens a person follows to finish one task.","w":[51.1,51.28,51.6,51.96,52.08,52.2,52.56,52.7,53.12,53.2,53.56,53.94,54.08,54.52,54.7]},{"s":2,"a":55.48,"b":60.69,"text":"A prototype is a version you can click through to test that flow before any code is written.","w":[55.56,55.7,56.72,56.84,56.94,57.32,57.46,57.68,57.96,58.24,58.42,58.7,58.92,59.22,59.7,59.94,60.24,60.36]},{"s":2,"a":60.99,"b":63.18,"text":"It can be paper screens you swap by hand.","w":[61.06,61.14,61.28,61.44,61.8,62.18,62.38,62.7,62.92]},{"s":2,"a":63.48,"b":66.25,"text":"Or screens linked in a design tool such as Figma.","w":[63.56,63.74,64.2,64.5,64.6,64.68,65.1,65.44,65.66,65.82]},{"s":2,"a":66.55,"b":69.49,"text":"This saves time and money before development begins.","w":[66.55,66.82,67.22,67.58,67.7,67.98,68.3,68.86]},{"s":2,"a":69.79,"b":71.05,"text":"The order of work is clear.","w":[69.79,69.96,70.2,70.32,70.6,70.74]},{"s":2,"a":71.35,"b":75.35,"text":"First the user flow, then sketches, then wireframes.","w":[71.42,71.72,71.9,72.16,72.96,73.26,74.3,74.56]},{"s":2,"a":75.65,"b":79.46,"text":"Then a prototype, then testing, then the visual design.","w":[75.68,75.88,75.96,77.02,77.26,78.26,78.5,78.6,78.96]},{"s":2,"a":79.76,"b":81.68,"text":"Each step builds on the one before.","w":[79.84,80.06,80.36,80.78,80.88,81.06,81.2]},{"s":3,"a":82.53,"b":84.73,"text":"Let us wireframe a login screen.","w":[82.56,82.76,82.94,83.78,83.86,84.28]},{"s":3,"a":85.03,"b":86.63,"text":"Put a logo box at the top.","w":[85.06,85.26,85.34,85.72,86.04,86.12,86.22]},{"s":3,"a":86.93,"b":89.95,"text":"Add two input boxes labelled email and password.","w":[87.04,87.3,87.62,87.94,88.42,88.86,89.26,89.4]},{"s":3,"a":90.25,"b":91.93,"text":"Add one clear main button.","w":[90.38,90.7,90.92,91.28,91.54]},{"s":3,"a":92.23,"b":94.45,"text":"Add a small link for forgotten password.","w":[92.34,92.52,92.64,93.08,93.34,93.5,93.9]},{"s":3,"a":94.75,"b":96.43,"text":"Keep the layout simple and clear.","w":[94.76,95,95.12,95.52,95.98,96.12]},{"s":3,"a":96.73,"b":99.41,"text":"Notice there is only one main action on this screen.","w":[96.84,97.2,97.38,97.52,97.9,98.08,98.42,98.76,98.86,99.02]},{"s":3,"a":99.71,"b":101.25,"text":"Then ask yourself a question.","w":[99.78,100.12,100.32,100.7,100.76]},{"s":3,"a":101.55,"b":103.94,"text":"What is the one thing the user came here to do?","w":[101.64,101.86,102,102.24,102.44,102.7,102.9,103.16,103.42,103.6,103.72]},{"s":3,"a":104.39,"b":106.53,"text":"Is it the most obvious thing on the screen?","w":[104.46,104.58,104.68,104.8,105.16,105.54,105.82,105.92,106.04]},{"s":4,"a":107.38,"b":108.02,"text":"Quick check.","w":[107.4,107.68]},{"s":4,"a":108.32,"b":110.8,"text":"You want to test whether people can find the checkout.","w":[108.34,108.5,108.72,108.84,109.16,109.42,109.7,109.88,110.14,110.24]},{"s":4,"a":111.1,"b":113.32,"text":"Do you need final colours and pictures first?","w":[111.1,111.2,111.34,111.64,112,112.4,112.54,112.92]},{"s":4,"a":113.77,"b":116.32,"text":"Pause here and try it. I'll wait.","w":[113.82,114.18,114.54,114.7,115.04,115.8,115.98]},{"s":5,"a":117.17,"b":117.47,"text":"No.","w":[117.24]},{"s":5,"a":117.77,"b":121.86,"text":"A rough clickable prototype is enough, and it is quicker to change.","w":[117.82,117.94,118.34,118.82,119.44,119.58,120.46,120.6,120.72,120.9,121.22,121.36]},{"s":6,"a":122.71,"b":129.47,"text":"One mistake is jumping straight to polished screens, or falling in love with the first idea. Start rough and test a second idea.","w":[122.86,123.02,123.48,123.62,124.02,124.3,124.42,124.84,125.48,125.64,125.98,126.1,126.3,126.42,126.54,126.82,127.74,128.04,128.36,128.48,128.72,128.82,129.14]},{"s":6,"a":129.77,"b":136.62,"text":"Another is cramming everything onto one screen. Keep one main job per screen. That keeps the main action obvious.","w":[129.84,130.22,130.4,130.94,131.46,131.86,132.06,132.98,133.32,133.5,133.74,134.04,134.3,134.84,135,135.26,135.38,135.72,136.1]},{"s":6,"a":136.92,"b":141.73,"text":"A third is designing screens without the flow between them. Map the user flow first.","w":[136.98,137.1,137.46,137.6,138.08,138.52,138.84,138.98,139.22,139.54,140.26,140.52,140.7,141,141.3]},{"s":7,"a":142.58,"b":143.21,"text":"Recap.","w":[142.66]},{"s":7,"a":143.51,"b":146.62,"text":"A wireframe shows structure, not colour.","w":[143.96,144.08,144.84,145.18,145.98,146.24]},{"s":7,"a":146.92,"b":149.56,"text":"A user flow is the path to finish one task.","w":[146.98,147.16,147.42,147.82,147.92,148.06,148.44,148.58,148.96,149.12]},{"s":7,"a":149.86,"b":152.84,"text":"A prototype lets you click through and test before code.","w":[149.96,150.06,150.68,150.9,151.06,151.32,151.7,151.86,152.2,152.54]},{"s":7,"a":153.14,"b":157.31,"text":"Top tip: ask what the one main job is, and make it obvious.","w":[153.18,153.48,154.42,154.66,154.84,155.06,155.24,155.5,155.82,156.34,156.48,156.66,156.78]},{"s":7,"a":157.61,"b":161.29,"text":"Keep practising with Knowzone, and you will design with confidence.","w":[157.62,157.9,158.46,158.66,159.56,159.7,159.82,160,160.44,160.62]}],"scenes":[{"at":0.25,"heading":"The puzzle","items":[{"at":0.4,"kind":"text","text":"Why is that button hard to find?"},{"at":6.12,"kind":"text","text":"Simple drawings + clickable drafts fix it before code"}]},{"at":12.62,"heading":"Wireframes","items":[{"at":12.77,"kind":"term","text":"Wireframe","detail":"Simple outline of a screen"},{"at":15.6,"kind":"text","text":"Boxes, lines, labels show what goes where"},{"at":20.49,"kind":"text","text":"No colours, real pictures or final fonts"},{"at":24.31,"kind":"term","text":"Like a blueprint","detail":"Shows the structure of a house, not the decoration"},{"at":26.7,"kind":"text","text":"Shows structure, not decoration"}]},{"at":29.13,"heading":"Fidelity","items":[{"at":29.28,"kind":"term","text":"Low fidelity","detail":"Rough and quick, like pencil and paper"},{"at":33.43,"kind":"term","text":"High fidelity","detail":"Close to the finished look"},{"at":39.29,"kind":"text","text":"Start rough: fast, cheap; 5 ideas in 10 min"},{"at":41.75,"kind":"text","text":"Feedback on structure, not colours"},{"at":46.43,"kind":"text","text":"Wireframe answers: what is this screen for?"}]},{"at":50.77,"heading":"Flow & prototype","items":[{"at":50.92,"kind":"term","text":"User flow","detail":"Path of screens to finish one task"},{"at":55.38,"kind":"term","text":"Prototype","detail":"Clickable version to test flow before code"},{"at":60.89,"kind":"text","text":"Paper screens swapped by hand"},{"at":63.38,"kind":"text","text":"Or linked screens in Figma"},{"at":66.45,"kind":"text","text":"Saves time + money before development"}]},{"at":69.54,"heading":"Order of work","items":[{"at":69.69,"kind":"text","text":"Work in this order:"},{"at":71.25,"kind":"text","text":"User flow → sketches → wireframes"},{"at":75.55,"kind":"text","text":"Prototype → testing → visual design"},{"at":79.66,"kind":"text","text":"Each step builds on the one before"}]},{"at":82.28,"heading":"Login wireframe","items":[{"at":84.93,"kind":"text","text":"Logo box at top"},{"at":86.83,"kind":"text","text":"2 input boxes: email, password"},{"at":90.15,"kind":"text","text":"1 clear main button"},{"at":92.13,"kind":"text","text":"Small forgotten-password link"},{"at":96.63,"kind":"text","text":"Simple + clear: only one main action"}]},{"at":99.46,"heading":"One main job","items":[{"at":99.61,"kind":"text","text":"Then ask yourself:"},{"at":101.45,"kind":"text","text":"What is the one thing the user came here to do?"},{"at":104.29,"kind":"text","text":"Is it the most obvious thing on the screen?"}]},{"at":106.95,"heading":"Quick check","items":[{"at":106.95,"kind":"question","text":"You want to test whether people can find the checkout. Do you need final colours and pictures first?"}]},{"at":116.92,"heading":"Answer","items":[{"at":117.07,"kind":"text","text":"No"},{"at":117.67,"kind":"text","text":"Rough clickable prototype is enough; quicker to change"}]},{"at":122.46,"heading":"Common mistakes","items":[{"at":122.61,"kind":"wrong","text":"Polish first / love first idea"},{"at":129.67,"kind":"wrong","text":"Cram everything onto one screen"},{"at":136.82,"kind":"wrong","text":"Design screens without the flow"}]},{"at":142.33,"heading":"Recap & top tip","items":[{"at":143.41,"kind":"text","text":"Wireframe: structure, not colour"},{"at":146.82,"kind":"text","text":"User flow: path to finish one task"},{"at":149.76,"kind":"text","text":"Prototype: click through + test before code"},{"at":153.04,"kind":"tip","text":"Ask what the one main job is, and make it obvious"},{"at":157.51,"kind":"text","text":"Keep practising with Knowzone"}]}],"check":{"at":116.57,"seconds":10,"question":"You want to test whether people can find the checkout. Do you need final colours and pictures first?","answer":"No. A rough clickable prototype is enough, and it is quicker to change."},"fps":30,"mouth":"","level":"","credits":[],"voice":"qwen3-tts-12hz-1.7b (cloned voice)"}